HID: magicmouse: one click per press on Apple SPI trackpads that hide report 0x21

Base: omacom/linux-aurora @ 78742b7013, drivers/hid/hid-magicmouse.c
Tested on: MacBook Pro 14" M1 Pro (apple,j314s), linux-aurora 7.2.11

With haptic_press=1 the driver derives the click from the summed finger
pressure and plays the click waveform itself. That only works if the
actuator is first told to stop clicking on its own (feature report 0x21,
"21 01" = host-controlled). On the J314 trackpad the actuator's HID
descriptor declares only input 0x3f and output 0x53, so the taptic helper
(hid-apple-mtp-haptic) decides the device has no mode report and returns
without sending anything. The firmware keeps its own click, and a firm press
vibrates twice: the driver's pulse at haptic_press_threshold and the
firmware's at its fixed threshold (about 125 on this machine).

The firmware does accept report 0x21 as a feature SET (not as an output
report) and answers a feature GET of it, although neither is declared. So:

- For SPI actuators whose descriptor lacks report 0x21, write the mode
  directly as a feature report and verify it by reading it back. Every other
  actuator still goes through apple_taptic_switch_modes() unchanged.
- Switch modes from a delayed work item, only while the pad is idle, with
  retries and backoff. Re-read the mode every 30 s of use and after a
  controller reset or resume, and take it again if the firmware dropped it.
- Exactly one click source at a time: the driver only plays waveforms and
  derives the button while host mode is confirmed. Until then, and whenever
  the switch fails, the firmware's own button and click are passed through.
- Hand the click back to the firmware (21 00) on teardown, and once
  haptic_press is turned off and userspace holds no force-feedback effect.
- Debounce the derived click (haptic_debounce_ms, default 40): the actuator
  shakes the pad, which made the pressure dip below the release threshold for
  a few milliseconds and registered a second click.
- haptic_trace logs every derived click transition and mode check.

